{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/368227-is-there-one-world-of-darkness-or-many","id":368227,"title":"Is there one World of Darkness or many?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-12T20:56:21-08:00","id":368227,"title":"Is there one World of Darkness or many?","content":"Just help me wrap my head around this. The various settings of the Classic World of Darkness stand alone mechanically, as they should (IMO), and because of that, and various other conflicting cosmological information between them, they should be considered separate worlds, or so seems to be the opinion of some on these forums. I agree that the various games set in the world of darkness tend to revolve around their own core themes, and it only muddies the waters of the games if you start trying to turn the World of Darkness into a RIFTS-style setting. None-the-less, crossovers were a constant fixture of the game until revised edition, and even then continued to have an impact on the greater World of Darkness, like the Week of Nightmares which affected Wraith, Vampire, <i>and</i> Mage.<br /> <br /> Werewolves do their thing, vampires do theirs, changelings do theirs, wraiths do theirs, and mages do whatever they heck they feel like, and because of that, all information that potentially links them to being in the same world should be ignored? It's just a multiverse with a bunch of coincidental crossovers that sound remarkably similar but really aren't the same thing at all? Is this the prevailing opinion on these things?<br /> <br /> Because we can find conflicting mechanics and cosmologies between the games doesn't mean the people at White Wolf weren't talking about the same place...they have far more in common than they have in conflict. Baba Yaga was a super-villain in both Werewolf and Vampire, and there is little doubt they are describing the same creature. The Shadow Lands as described by the vampires calling themselves the Harbingers of Skulls seem remarkably similar to the Shadow Lands described in Wraith. The Tremere (one of the core clans of Vampire) were once part of the Order of Hermes (one of the core traditions of Mage) and both settings mention one another. Many people seem to want to ignore these overlapping aspects the various games. I just don't understand why.<br /> <br /> Yes it's true that anyone running a Werewolf game is probably better off avoiding crossovers with the other settings at their gaming tables. Reconciling the mechanical differences between the settings is a pain in the ass, and little is gained by dipping one's toes into the other lines since the conflicting themes make for bad stories. Let's face it, Werewolf games are about entirely different things than Mage games and introducing mages to a Werewolf game (or vice versa) detracts from the core themes that make each of those games what they are. It still doesn't change that fact that the metaplot of the Classic World of Darkness included both lines in the ongoing and evolving events of a shared world.<br /> <br /> It sure stinks that Baba Yaga was killed on the Vampire end of things for the Werewolf fans, but she was part of that setting too. It's the Wraith players that really have reason to gripe; their game was essentially destroyed by events occurring in a Vampire book. Yep, people ignored it, and kept playing as though the 6<sup>th</sup> Great Maelstrom never happened, and who could blame them? I'm a fan of many of the game lines, and I also dislike how often they constantly screwed with one another like many other people do. I'm of the belief that these ongoing metaplot crossovers were a big factor in the decision to end the Classic World of Darkness and start fresh.<br /> <br /> I might just be some crotchety old fart that refuses to subscribe to the revisionist history others prefer despite the probability that it makes their games run smoother. Maybe I shouldn't stubbornly cling to past <i>truths</i> and embrace this new view of the old setting. I might have some sick attachment to the way things were because of my love of the old World of Darkness and the nostalgia I feel whenever I play it. Am I completely off my rocker, or are there other people on these forums that share my view on this?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3474-nastynate","name":"nastynate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T22:12:35-08:00","id":368283,"title":"","content":"TBH, I would like to point out that the writers pretty much painted themselves into a corner. They set every game as &quot;one week away from the end of it all&quot; and this meant that they had to do the endgame scenario. Now, I was irked that the end of the Wraith line was due to the hands of the other lines. I feel that each line should have ended itself. I can see that they way they did it was to go &quot;Yes, these lines all exist in one single cosmos.&quot;<br /> So, to your point about all of this being in separate universes? I have to say that the Week of Nightmares says no. The rules gave someone a headache to try to blend it all together. My group had to come to a discussion before we could agree how Celerity and Rage interacted with one another. Many games of Soul Blade were had when rules disputes came up. Yes, we did trial by combat via Soul Blade when a peaceful ending could not be done. But that is a story for another day.<br /> In any event, did they all exist? Yes. Was it a good idea to have any of them interact in practice? NOOOOOOOOOOOOOPE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T22:19:29-08:00","id":368289,"title":"","content":"Each game is basically its own different take on the setting. Some games don't presume too much about the cosmology of their setting, and they can get along fairly well with others, like Hunter&quot; the Reckoning, and to a lesser extent, Mummy, Wraith and Changeling. Others can't have any sort of accord of harmony between them, with the outstanding example of Werewolf and Mage. Vampire and Werewolf also disagree vehemently, and Vampire's crossover mechanics of &quot;highest dot rating wins&quot; could really be seen to universally be shit by players of all other games. Demon doesn't seem like it was every meant to be played with anything else.<br /> <br /> Some people will disagree and cite very early books. Generally, however, this was killed hard post-Chaos Factor and soulforged into an ashtray; by the time Revised came about, every game basically took its balls and went home. There was something to the effect of &quot;multiple worlds&quot; to explain many of the inconsistencies in Mage's capstone book Ascension, too. Basically, while there might be some major events that echo through every WoD, each WoD is its own and exists independently of the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T22:35:26-08:00","id":368303,"title":"","content":"Each MAJOR game line existed in it's own world. There were crossover books but each of the main game lines effectively exist in their own world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T23:46:33-08:00","id":368346,"title":"","content":"The games are toolkits some authors think Crossover is the most awesome thing ever. Others hate it like the plague. Piece together the world that works best for you and to hell with anyone trying to say something &quot;many bubbles theory&quot; is canon, you bought the books read them how you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T23:54:25-08:00","id":368356,"title":"","content":"This recently came up in another thread so just adding my opinion quickly here that the Worlds of Darkness work best as separate entities, though crossover is completely manageable <i>if</i> you want to work for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T01:42:25-08:00","id":368422,"title":"","content":"Mage posited the WoD as a series of overlapping parallel realities with varying degrees of bleedthrough from one to the other. That's the model I use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T02:11:00-08:00","id":368450,"title":"","content":"I think 'Mostly Harmless' (the last HHGttG book - 'And Another Thing' is an abomination that I shall not acknowledge) posits a cosmology that best sums up the differentiation between cWoD game worlds - the Whole Sort of General Mish-Mash. Essentially the entire cWoD is a single universe but it is too complex to all be perceived simultaneously so it must be sliced to make sense of. The core game lines present relatively narrow slices with only the bare bones of other lines represented. Supplements show wider slices that may include some of the other lines flesh.<br /> <br /> One of the interesting effects of this approach is it allows one slice (gameline) to be affected by something that doesn't really work within its own lore, allowing crossover madness such as Sam.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/757-filli-noctus","name":"filli noctus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T06:09:38-08:00","id":368556,"title":"","content":"Of course, there's only one World of Darkness<br /> all the beings are there (as you can see reading some books, and I'm not speaking stricly of the crossovers, but even certain splatbook, core books of the minor lines [mummy, kote, kotek]), but usually they don't interact too much...<br /> <br /> There're usually 3 major faults people point in this reasonment:<br /> <br /> 1. The system are totally different<br /> 2. In the books they say &quot;other than what we're writing here, don't care of others line&quot;<br /> 3. The pantheon are totally different<br /> <br /> <br /> (1) and (2) got a simple interpretation, simply the authors don't want you to go around buying 500 hundreds of books, usually is specified that you need only the core book of that line to play (with the addition of the sourcebook YOU wanted to buy maybe and a couple books if the concept is quite advanced, for example the addition of VtM, Blood Magic for VtM, Blood Sacrifice). It's a clever choice, as minimizing the minimal requirement for playing let you enlarge the human gaming base (and even more clever if you want to &quot;attack&quot; a gaming base not really wealthy or already interested in some other game line [like D&amp;D]). In the end, it's an unorthodox strategic move.<br /> <br /> (3) is relative to how the WW developed. At a certain time there were a lot of authors working on something like 5 o 6 lines, and sometimes even the material from the same line contradicted each other, because they were written by different individuals at different times, and they could not be expected to take into account of the entire amount of books written precedently written. Someone is saying VtM: Blood Bond or VtM: Diablerie Mexico are not canon because they treat blood bonds differently from the corebooks? Nope.<br /> The main point is, if you can't or don't want to device your own version of the cosmological situation, the real version is the one of the game line you're playing. They're explicitly opposed, each line had 2 or 3 main editions, if at a certain point they wanted to retcon all in a single origin, they would have done.<br /> You're playing Werewolf? Then the vampires ARE a vicious strain of wyrm-ridden corpses... you want to add the vampiric lore? of course, in the beginning there was only on vampire, created by 1 or 2 of the heads of the wyrm... he created others vampire and every time that the curse is transmitted, it weakens. Done, here's the whole vampiric cosmology retconned.<br /> All the events happen in the same cursed world, but the different beings see differt facets even when they call them in the same way. I remember even a curious statement in Gehenna (now, if you just count to seven, someone will jump out shouting &quot;Gehenna is not canon!&quot; despite the fact it was the conclusive book of a game-line :P ), it said something like &quot;And what about werewolves, mages and all the other beings in the World of Darkness? They're occupied with their own apocalypses, don't bother with them if you don't want to throw them in the central stage of your own End of Times&quot; [Mind you, it's just an outline of what I remember without recovering the book, and on top, it's translated from my own language; the actual English version may be slightly different].<br /> <br /> In the end, yes. Is the same world, but is the Storyteller the one that decide what is real","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T07:07:50-08:00","id":368585,"title":"","content":"Is there one World of Darkness or many?<br /> <br /> Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T12:13:17-08:00","id":368823,"title":"","content":"The way I think of it is, each game line in oWoD is part of a single game universe--but as described by an unreliable narrator. Other systems are misinterpreted or neglected because they aren't so relevant to whoever's telling the story, or they are flat-out wrong for dramatic or ideological purposes. If you want to combine the stories and suss out the &quot;truth&quot;, cool, but you are playing anthropologist and can't ever verify that your theory is the one true fact. The best you can do is to write something that will keep the grumbling to a minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T12:17:11-08:00","id":368828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/368227-is-there-one-world-of-darkness-or-many?p=368823#post368823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you want to combine the stories and suss out the &quot;truth&quot;, cool, but you are playing anthropologist and can't ever verify that your theory is the one true fact. The best you can do is to write something that will keep the grumbling to a minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you are a Mage player, in which case you got every cosmological knot figured out and are rather smug about it :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T12:51:50-08:00","id":368857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/368227-is-there-one-world-of-darkness-or-many?p=368828#post368828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless you are a Mage player, in which case you got every cosmological knot figured out and are rather smug about it :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Until you get dumped into a Werewolf-dominated corner of the metacosmos, where you find that Everything You Know Is Wrong. Just forget the words and sing along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T16:10:57-08:00","id":369110,"title":"","content":"There is only one World of Darkness, hence the name of the whole thing World of Darkness not Worlds of Darkness a big difference in only a single letter. If they would have wanted it to be worlds they could easily have done it while doing the revised thing as they changed plenty of other, including major, things then but they didn't it remained a singular World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> When I ST I take into consideration how major actions affect this group or that cross-the-lines and within. I do think it makes for a much larger and more layered world.<br /> <br /> In the end like I said in another thread there is more evidence on the side of the one world theory than there is against it. The conflicting issues are mostly mythological or naming issues easily explained by misunderstandings and point of view especially since most of those are related to issues no one can verify. Vampiric mythos is tied to Christianity yes, currently, but most pre-Christian elders might not exactly buy that line and there is precious little proof of it's validity, they are stories that is all. Garou tell a different tale colored by their finite lifespans and what ever stories the spirits tell them, colored by the spirits nature, point of view and mostly told in metaphor easily misinterpreted. Mages are often, quite a bit more often that they would ever admit, blinded by their own hubris, once one knows the truth all others must be wrong and they have fought entire wizardly wars over these matters.Where as there is actual solid evidence of them all existing in a single world, Tremere/Order of Hermes, Changelings/Fianna, Shadowlords/Tzimisce, Silent Striders/Followers of Set, Nagaraja/Chackravanti, Giovanni/Wraith, Keremet &amp; Sluagh/Wraith, Kiasyd/Changeling, Mummy/Setites &amp; Siletn Striders &amp; Mokole &amp; Bubasti &amp; Children of Osiris &amp; Mages, Abominations etc. I could go on and on with examples where the lines cross in a way that affect both which only makes sense, especially since these are not once in a blue moon crossings but enduring things like Setites eternal war on Striders and Giovanni's constant connections to Wraiths or the ongoing conflict between the Order of Hermes and Tremere, if they all happen in the same world. Even Demon the Fallen with all it's faults, it only had one edition or 1.5 if you count Devil's Due, kinda forced the issue on multiple occasions as many other lines bad guys were, in those lines I might add, retconned into being DtF Demons or Earthbound. Also worth mentioning is taht one of the sample Earthbound in their own book was a former servant of Baba Yaga nicely tying even DtF to Vampire and Werewolf both of which were familiar with the Methuselah.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> I almost forgot the important thing to remember is that you can choose otherwise at your table like with anything else. This of course does not mean that it is anything but your own house-ruling which means it should be kept at the table or clearly announced to be an in-house ruling in discussions cause nothing is quite more disrupting for a conversation about how two different supernatural get along, or not as the case most of the time is, than silly claims of them existing in different worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":". 01-13-2015, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T16:54:51-08:00","id":369163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/368227-is-there-one-world-of-darkness-or-many?p=369110#post369110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is only one World of Darkness, hence the name of the whole thing World of Darkness not Worlds of Darkness a big difference in only a single letter. If they would have wanted it to be worlds they could easily have done it while doing the revised thing as they changed plenty of other, including major, things then but they didn't it remained a singular World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it could be that when you're playing, it is typically in a single WoD. Taglines aren't actually terrible persuasive evidence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I ST I take into consideration how major actions affect this group or that cross-the-lines and within. I do think it makes for a much larger and more layered world.<br /> <br /> In the end like I said in another thread there is more evidence on the side of the one world theory than there is against it. The conflicting issues are mostly mythological or naming issues easily explained by misunderstandings and point of view especially since most of those are related to issues no one can verify. Vampiric mythos is tied to Christianity yes, currently, but most pre-Christian elders might not exactly buy that line and there is precious little proof of it's validity, they are stories that is all. </div> </div> </div>Except when the game gets railroaded into a full-on, &quot;this is the real truth of the game line&quot; Noddist Gehenna. Or when sources from a wide variety of different games lay on stuff out of character, with not unreliable narrator to worry about. Or when there are radically different crossover rules in each Storyteller's Handbook. Vampire says &quot;highest level power wins&quot;, Werewolf gives it the finger and says &quot;roll Willpower or find the nearest equivalent; the Vampire rules are terrible and make no sense for this game.&quot;<br /> .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Garou tell a different tale colored by their finite lifespans and what ever stories the spirits tell them, colored by the spirits nature, point of view and mostly told in metaphor easily misinterpreted. Mages are often, quite a bit more often that they would ever admit, blinded by their own hubris, once one knows the truth all others must be wrong and they have fought entire wizardly wars over these matters.Where as there is actual solid evidence of them all existing in a single world, Tremere/Order of Hermes, Changelings/Fianna, Shadowlords/Tzimisce, Silent Striders/Followers of Set, Nagaraja/Chackravanti, Giovanni/Wraith, Keremet &amp; Sluagh/Wraith, Kiasyd/Changeling, Mummy/Setites &amp; Siletn Striders &amp; Mokole &amp; Bubasti &amp; Children of Osiris &amp; Mages, Abominations etc. I could go on and on with examples where the lines cross in a way that affect both which only makes sense, especially since these are not once in a blue moon crossings but enduring things like Setites eternal war on Striders and Giovanni's constant connections to Wraiths or the ongoing conflict between the Order of Hermes and Tremere, if they all happen in the same world. </div> </div> </div>1 - taking a tack that undercuts strong thematic elements of all games benefits none of them.<br /> <br /> 2 - The lines had a lot more interaction very early on. However, the writing approach changed dramatically between editions, and there have been plenty of retcons to distance each line from each other. The first editions might have been taking place in the same world, or not, but the Revised and Anniversary editions certainly aren't tying your hands to a single world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even Demon the Fallen with all it's faults, it only had one edition or 1.5 if you count Devil's Due, kinda forced the issue on multiple occasions as many other lines bad guys were, in those lines I might add, retconned into being DtF Demons or Earthbound. Also worth mentioning is taht one of the sample Earthbound in their own book was a former servant of Baba Yaga nicely tying even DtF to Vampire and Werewolf both of which were familiar with the Methuselah. </div> </div> </div>If you want it to, it can. But it's from first edition, so it doesn't tie them together strongly. Word of Gods on the subject is that the lines don't inherently work together, after all; the only intention was that they would collapse if all taken together, and you'd have to make up a world that suits you. Hence, there is no single canon WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT:<br /> I almost forgot the important thing to remember is that you can choose otherwise at your table like with anything else. This of course does not mean that it is anything but your own house-ruling which means it should be kept at the table or clearly announced to be an in-house ruling in discussions cause nothing is quite more disrupting for a conversation about how two different supernatural get along, or not as the case most of the time is, than silly claims of them existing in different worlds. </div> </div> </div>House rules are required for some of the games to interact at all. For Werewolf and Mage, someone has to be wrong, or you have to make something up to take another option. You cannot harmoniously weld together a game that assumes the physical world is vast and stretches on in infinity, as science has discovered, while another says that science is another type of magic, baby, and everything past the asteroid belt is the Deep Umbra! Because in Werewolf, the Deep Umbra is some kind of weird otherrealm, while all of the spiritual reflection of the universe away from Earth is the Aetherial Realm, making the Penumbra much, much larger in one game than the other. Other regions of the Umbra don't need to be the same as in another game, either, and the Dreaming is pretty much inaccessible to anyone but Changelings, which means that it's so out of focus it might as well just not exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T16:56:11-08:00","id":369164,"title":"","content":"It's not a houserule if you're playing Mage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T18:42:46-08:00","id":369273,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">One or many? <br /> Depends on the game and the troupe.<br /> Personally, I treat the different settings as bits and pieces of mise-en-scene; whatever sets the stage in ways players find more enjoyable.<br /> <br /> As far as crossovers go, I have a laundry list of adjustments and tweaks that I use to make different games jive with one another, but \u2013 like I said \u2013 that depends on the game and the troupe. <br /> <br /> Short answer: Meh. It depends. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T07:54:36-08:00","id":369744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/368227-is-there-one-world-of-darkness-or-many?p=369164#post369164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a houserule if you're playing Mage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing is a house rule in Mage. One way or another, it's just a rule interpretation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T12:07:09-08:00","id":369972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The lines had a lot more interaction very early on. However, the writing approach changed dramatically between editions, and there have been plenty of retcons to distance each line from each other. The first editions might have been taking place in the same world, or not, but the Revised and Anniversary editions certainly aren't tying your hands to a single world. </div> </div> </div>Maybe this is part of my disconnect. I tend to think of 1st and 2nd edition as the meat and potatoes of the World of Darkness. It may just be how it seemed to me, but it felt like more books were published for 2nd edition than every other edition combined, and that 1993 to 1998 was the golden age of White Wolf (in terms of publishing volume, number of players, and influence on the gaming industry - revised had better writing and book quality on the whole). If your impression of the classic World of Darkness is based on Revised edition and later and you place less emphasis on the hundred of books already published to that point, I can see where you would get a different feel from the game.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3474-nastynate","name":"nastynate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T12:50:30-08:00","id":370030,"title":"","content":"Considering that Dark Alliance, Under a Blood Red Moon and Chaos Factor all had consequences that carried on into later editions of the involved game lines I'm of the opinion that there was one CWoD and all the various factions have limited perceptions of the bigger overall picture, interpreted through their species specific lens. I'm also a proponent of Exalted 1st ed being the pre-history of the CWoD, which it was advertised as being when it first launched, all of their splats having intentionally specific analogues in the CWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T14:46:00-08:00","id":370147,"title":"","content":"I personally like to run them as separate; a <i>Vampire </i>game might have lupines and ghosts, but they're not going to be as fleshed out as proper Werewolves and Wraiths. I feel like trying to make the whole crossover thing work is kinda like eating soup with a fork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T18:35:28-08:00","id":370524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nastynate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/368227-is-there-one-world-of-darkness-or-many?p=369972#post369972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe this is part of my disconnect. I tend to think of 1st and 2nd edition as the meat and potatoes of the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't. Shit was all about Vampire and Mage and squeezing everything else out for importance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It may just be how it seemed to me, but it felt like more books were published for 2nd edition than every other edition combined, and that 1993 to 1998 was the golden age of White Wolf (in terms of publishing volume, number of players, and influence on the gaming industry - revised had better writing and book quality on the whole). If your impression of the classic World of Darkness is based on Revised edition and later and you place less emphasis on the hundred of books already published to that point, I can see where you would get a different feel from the game. </div> </div> </div>More like golden age of the supplement treadmill. Now everyone can take a step back and concentrate on the strengths of the line in the line proper, and not have to bend over backward to make everything sync up to the other games. Edit: We can also avoid horrid mistakes. WoD: Gypsies, the original Fianna and Get of Fenris Tribebooks, the poor editing in the old Shadow Lords tribebook that had them using the Mokole's word for other shapeshifters, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T21:25:30-08:00","id":370748,"title":"","content":"Woah, hold on there... Vampire came first and was the most popular of the World of Darkness games, so of course it got the most attention. Mage was a surprise success, and got quite few books too, but I'm pretty sure Werewolf was number two in terms of splats and had it's fair share of fans, though whether or not it was more or less popular than Mage in the end I'm not really certain. Wraith and Changeling never had much traction, and neither got a Revised edition core book (Wraith ended completely and abruptly in 1999). So yeah 2nd edition was the golden age of the supplement treadmill, which just so happened to coincide with the most players and consumers of the product line. Try telling a Wraith player that Revised edition was better.<br /> <br /> Furthermore Revised didn't come along and replace everything that came before it. Revised was a continuation of the <i>same</i> setting and metaplot. It was an attempt to clean up the rules, and change the focus, but it wasn't wiping the slate clean and starting over. All those terrible books you're citing were part of the revised setting too, out-dated and awful, but still part of it. You can add numerous others to the list if you want to, though Revised had it's share of stinkers as well. I think you're confusing Revised with the New World of Darkness. That was where White Wolf got the chance to revisit their mistakes, wipe the slate clean, and do things over differently.<br /> <br /> 1st, 2nd, and Revised were all part of the same Classic World of Darkness setting, not individual reboots of the game lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that Dark Alliance, Under a Blood Red Moon and Chaos Factor all had consequences that carried on into later editions of the involved game lines I'm of the opinion that there was one CWoD and all the various factions have limited perceptions of the bigger overall picture, interpreted through their species specific lens. I'm also a proponent of Exalted 1st ed being the pre-history of the CWoD, which it was advertised as being when it first launched, all of their splats having intentionally specific analogues in the CWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely how I interpret things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3474,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3474-nastynate","user":"nastynate","date":". 01-15-2015, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3474-nastynate","name":"nastynate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T22:21:12-08:00","id":370761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nastynate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/368227-is-there-one-world-of-darkness-or-many?p=370748#post370748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woah, hold on there...</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Chaining things to Vampire just because it's the first game is a terrible way to go. It came first? Great, it has the most mistakes and retcons. Retcons which went from a setting where Vicissitude was a disease and the Tal'Mahe'Ra were saving us all to a setting where Vicissitude was just a Discipline and the Tal'Mahe'Ra were a bunch of nutcases out to try and wrest power, just like every other vampire faction in existence. Or how about the Salubri? Super-rare, always kind healers. Except not, because there was a parallel Clan of warriors that embraces like there's no tomorrow and wants the Tremere to die. Golconda? Maybe, maybe not.<br /> <br /> I don't even think that there's a single unified world for each setting, at this point. Maybe it's like the relationship the BattleTech cartoon has to the actual setting - fiction within fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 01-15-2015, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T03:07:15-08:00","id":370840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/368227-is-there-one-world-of-darkness-or-many?p=370147#post370147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally like to run them as separate; a <i>Vampire </i>game might have lupines and ghosts, but they're not going to be as fleshed out as proper Werewolves and Wraiths. I feel like trying to make the whole crossover thing work is kinda like eating soup with a fork.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wrap the noodles around the fork and drink the soup from the bowl. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:59:40-08:00","id":371093,"title":"","content":"Or eat Chunky, the soup that eats like a meal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T09:27:32-08:00","id":371111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/368227-is-there-one-world-of-darkness-or-many?p=370761#post370761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Chaining things to Vampire just because it's the first game is a terrible way to go. It came first? Great, it has the most mistakes and retcons. Retcons which went from a setting where Vicissitude was a disease and the Tal'Mahe'Ra were saving us all to a setting where Vicissitude was just a Discipline and the Tal'Mahe'Ra were a bunch of nutcases out to try and wrest power, just like every other vampire faction in existence. Or how about the Salubri? Super-rare, always kind healers. Except not, because there was a parallel Clan of warriors that embraces like there's no tomorrow and wants the Tremere to die. Golconda? Maybe, maybe not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said Vampire got the most books and attention because it came first and was the most popular. It was around longer than the others and was the most popular of the Classic World of Darkness game lines so naturally it got the lion's share of the setting's focus. Being in publication the longest + being the best seller = largest library of books; it's also natural that it had the most mistakes and retcons because it had the most books. You're only supporting my assertion by pointing that out.<br /> <br /> What's wrong with the most popular games and the best sellers getting the most books and attention? Without the popular titles and their success we'd have never gotten the hidden gems like Wraith which were bankrolled by Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage. If Mummy turned out to be the best seller, we'd have had a Classic World of Darkness flooded with Mummy books. The classic World of Darkness setting was shackled to the big three titles because the big three were the cash cows that kept White Wolf in business. How can anyone begrudge White Wolf for catering to their largest group of consumers? That's pretty normal behavior for a business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3474,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3474-nastynate","user":"nastynate","date":". 01-15-2015, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3474-nastynate","name":"nastynate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T10:50:46-08:00","id":371234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nastynate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/368227-is-there-one-world-of-darkness-or-many?p=371111#post371111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I said Vampire got the most books and attention because it came first and was the most popular. It was around longer than the others and was the most popular of the Classic World of Darkness game lines so naturally it got the lion's share of the setting's focus. Being in publication the longest + being the best seller = largest library of books; it's also natural that it had the most mistakes and retcons because it had the most books. You're only supporting my assertion by pointing that out.<br /> <br /> What's wrong with the most popular games and the best sellers getting the most books and attention? Without the popular titles and their success we'd have never gotten the hidden gems like Wraith which were bankrolled by Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage. If Mummy turned out to be the best seller, we'd have had a Classic World of Darkness flooded with Mummy books. The classic World of Darkness setting was shackled to the big three titles because the big three were the cash cows that kept White Wolf in business. How can anyone begrudge White Wolf for catering to their largest group of consumers? That's pretty normal behavior for a business.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about metaplot events and rules interactions here, not raw time and money spent on producing content. Vampire and Mage, then later Demon, tried to make everything in their individual games a Big Deal, and went far over the top to do it. Everything else pretty much stayed pretty calm until the very end. At the very least, those two blocks could be considered to be existing in at least two different worlds - &quot;Loud Metaplot&quot; and &quot;Quiet Metaplot&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T02:50:49-07:00","id":494533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/368227-is-there-one-world-of-darkness-or-many?p=368283#post368283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TBH, I would like to point out that the writers pretty much painted themselves into a corner. They set every game as &quot;one week away from the end of it all&quot; and this meant that they had to do the endgame scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel compelled to point out, whenever this comes up, that the notion that White Wolf <b>had to end the game lines</b> is a bit of carefully crafted revisionism perpetrated by the developers and continued by the more devout members of the fan base.<br /> <br /> When they announced the end of the Classic World of Darkness lines, the developers at White Wolf spun the decision as something they had promised the fans since day one. Essentially, they were saying &quot;We've been talking about the end of the world in our games since the first edition of Vampire, so we're finally giving you what you've been asking for! Isn't that great!&quot;<br /> <br /> Except no one was asking for the game lines to end. While people were certainly excited to see what books like Gehenna and Apocalypse would be like, no one was really out there demanding these books be written.<br /> <br /> For that matter they had never promised these end of the world books. Quite the contrary - at least one of the Vampire developers had gone on record during an interview in the mid to late 90's saying that they would never write a Gehenna book. Of course, management changes, markets change, and if there's one thing I learned as a fan of White Wolf's games, it's that any time they said publicly they weren't going to do something, you could bet they'd do it at some point or other.<br /> <br /> There was no pressing, narrative need to end the cWoD game lines, as evidenced by the existence and success of the 20th Anniversary editions and the accompanying new material that has been released. Gehenna still works just fine as a narrative tool in V20 as it did in 1st Edition - each troupe is capable of making up their own minds about the truth of the Gehenna Prophecies or what have you. <br /> <br /> In the end, the decision to create the nWoD games came down to money and company politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:50:28-07:00","id":494963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/368227-is-there-one-world-of-darkness-or-many?p=494533#post494533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter they had never promised these end of the world books. Quite the contrary - at least one of the Vampire developers had gone on record during an interview in the mid to late 90's saying that they would never write a Gehenna book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was actually Justin Achilli, it was his first Developer Chat on the old White Wolf site, and I have no doubt he believed that at the time, and you can find it in the Wayback Machine. I'm on my phone or I would provide links.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T15:10:11-07:00","id":495256,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much! I remember reading the article but it was years ago and I could never find it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T15:30:22-07:00","id":495295,"title":"","content":"Necro-Necro-Necro-Necro...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thank